<!-- CONTEXT: THE SAVE SYSTEM -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-network-wired"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">How It Works: The Save System</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="info-content">
        <p>You do <strong>not</strong> need to write any file handling code. The Engine does the heavy lifting for you.</p>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
            <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center;">
                <span class="badge" style="background: #28a745; color: white; padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 4px;">SAVING</span>
                <span>The Engine asks your player object: <em>"Give me a dictionary of your stats."</em> (<code style="color: #d63384;">to_save_data</code>). The Engine then writes that dictionary to a file.</span>
            </div>
            <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center;">
                <span class="badge" style="background: #007bff; color: white; padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 4px;">LOADING</span>
                <span>The Engine reads the file, gets the dictionary, and hands it to your class: <em>"Build a new player from this data."</em> (<code style="color: #d63384;">from_save_data</code>).</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">Your job is just to pack the suitcase (dictionary) and unpack it. The Engine carries it to the airport (File System).</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- STRUCTURE GUIDE -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Structure Guide</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p class="section-intro">Implement these hooks to let the engine save your game.</p>
    
    <!-- 1. to_save_data -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">to_save_data (Instance Method)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD to_save_data() → dict:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                Return a dictionary containing all stats needed to restore the player:
                <ul>
                    <li>name, player_type, health, max_health, armour, accuracy</li>
                    <li>inventory (list of items)</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="skeleton-line code" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">RETURN { "name": self.name, ... }</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 2. from_save_data -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">from_save_data (@classmethod)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">@CLASSMETHOD</div>
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD from_save_data(cls, data) → Player:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Important:</strong> This creates a NEW player.
                <ol>
                    <li>Create instance: <code>player = cls(data["name"])</code></li>
                    <li>Restore functionality: calls <code>__init__</code> automatically</li>
                    <li>Overwrite stats: <code>player.health = data["health"]</code>, etc.</li>
                    <li>Restore inventory: Loop through <code>data["inventory"]</code> and add items</li>
                    <li>Return the new player object</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

